# LiNC simulation-only panel wiring.
#
# Loaded after linc.hal (which creates cnc_panel.*) and before the display.
# The reference baiermill_sim HAL replaces the physical cabinet wiring with
# rio.sim-* inputs; these nets connect the LiNC panel service to that simulated
# hardware. Do not load this file on a real machine.

# E-stop mushroom: cnc_panel.estop is the mushroom state.
net sim-estop cnc_panel.estop => rio.sim-estop

# Momentary POWER ON / POWER OFF keys. A POWER ON also resets a latched E-stop
# before rio.sim-power-on latches the machine switch.
#
# Releasing the E-stop mushroom raises its own one-shot (`cnc_panel.estop_reset`)
# so the controller leaves E-stop without the machine being powered up. Both
# sources are ORed: `halui.estop.reset` is a single pin.
# or2.estop_reset is created in linc.hal (or2 is loaded once there).
addf or2.estop_reset servo-thread
# `halui.estop.reset` leaves the task in ESTOP_RESET, which enables motion but is
# not the ON state: `EMC_JOINT_HOME` (and other task commands) refuse it with
# "cannot be executed until the machine is out of E-stop and turned on". Jogging
# works in that state, which is why homing after a jog was the first failure.
net sim-power-on cnc_panel.power_on => rio.sim-power-on or2.estop_reset.in0 halui.machine.on
net sim-estop-reset cnc_panel.estop_reset => or2.estop_reset.in1
net estop-reset-request or2.estop_reset.out => halui.estop.reset
net sim-power-off cnc_panel.power_off => rio.sim-power-off halui.machine.off
